`EnsureInitialized()` checks the window and clears the samples; every other call returns `Error::NotInitialized`
until it has succeeded.

## What it does

- `xmpl100::MovingAverage<N>`: the mean of the last samples in fixed storage (the template's example utility).
- One include root, `@ROOT@/`, and one CMake target, `xmpl100::xmpl100`.
- Every fallible call returns `Result<T>` with an `Error`: no exceptions, no heap, no RTTI.
- MCU-agnostic: the same code on any MCU and on the host (`examples/host`).

## Install

```bash
git submodule add https://github.com/@ORG@/@REPO@.git external/@REPO@
```

```cmake
add_subdirectory(external/@REPO@)
target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE xmpl100::xmpl100)
```

Details: [Integration](docs/integration.md) and [Platforms](docs/platforms.md).

